 - For a session that completes without error the hooks fire in the order `beforeSession` → `beforeUserInput` → `afterUserInput` → `beforeModelResponse` → `afterModelResponse` → `afterSession` ([validated by: fires the lifecycle hooks in documented order for a session that completes without error](../../src/config.test.ts#L132)).
 - A `beforeSession` that throws reaches the caller as a rejection, and also runs `onError` with the thrown error and then `afterSession`, because the call sits inside the same `try`/`finally` as the rest of the turn. An `afterSession` hook called under this condition can infer the session never advanced past `beforeSession`: no user-input hooks ran, no model response was generated, and no tool rounds were started — a cleanup hook that allocates in `beforeSession` and frees in `afterSession` will therefore always see the allocation and the release on the same error path ([validated by: runs onError then afterSession when it throws, and still rejects to the caller](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L116)).
 
+## Usage reported to afterModelResponse
+
+- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message, after the round loop exits, and is handed the usage summed across every provider call the turn made, tool rounds included, so a deployer billing or budgeting from the hook counts the whole turn ([validated by: reports the sum of every provider call in a turn that ran two tool rounds](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.usage.acceptance.test.ts#L74)).
+- The sum adds `inputTokens`, `outputTokens`, and `totalTokens` independently across the rounds that reported usage ([validated by: sums token counts from two rounds](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L29)).
+- A round that reports no usage adds nothing to that sum ([validated by: counts the rounds that reported usage, skipping rounds that reported none](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.usage.acceptance.test.ts#L80)).
+- A turn in which no round reported passes `undefined` ([validated by: reports nothing when no round in the turn reported usage](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.usage.acceptance.test.ts#L85)).
+- A turn that makes no tool call passes exactly the usage its single provider call reported, as it did before the sum was introduced ([validated by: receives collected response text and usage](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L236)).
+
 ## Engine startup
 
 - The engine's `start()` method rejects the returned promise when it cannot bind the configured port, rather than emitting an unhandled error event that would take the process down ([validated by: rejects instead of taking the process down with an unhandled error event](../../src/config.test.ts#L174)).
 
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
-These two properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
